Z||000000||DavidHenshaw||05-27-2001||10:41 PM||||Where is the cheapest place to buy the trunk weatherstrip. Fiero store wants $80 unless they have gone up and I think the local GM dealer quoted $90 to a $100.<P>My present weather strip is in real bad shape. From the design of the trunk weatherstrip area on my 86 GT fastback it appears even a new weatherstrip won't keep out all the water.<P>Dave<P>86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||05-27-2001||11:00 PM||||I'm sure you can find a decent one in a junkyard for much cheaper, or maybe someone around here has a good one for sale.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000002||btoth||05-28-2001||12:18 PM||||My trunk on my GT was still leaking after i replaced the weather stripping and the spoiler gaskets.  I made sure that I used enough sealant, too.  Turns out I have a rusted spot near my driver-side wheel well which needs to be fixed.  Check under your carpeting before you glue a new weatherstrip down.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
